        <mxCell id="framec126" value="spk" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=7;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="690" y="954" width="40" height="12" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="framec127" value="F1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=8;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="476" y="1054" width="60" height="10" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="framec128" value="F2" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=8;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="744" y="1054" width="60" height="10" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="framec129" value="&lt;b&gt;BUILD&lt;/b&gt;  1. Cut five 90 × 70 dot boards (TA1057) with a knife along a hole row: F1, F2 60 × 60, T1, T2 90 × 60, MB 74 × 40. 2. Ø1.5 holes with bit TA0149. tronic.lk's bits stop at 1.5 mm, so open the Ø3 / Ø3.2 holes with a 3 mm hand drill or round needle file (hardware shop). Cut the window: drill its corners, then knife. 3. Screw each post together: one F-F 20 (TA1043) then six M-F 12 (TA1034). 4. Bolt F1 and F2 to the posts: M3 × 10 bolt + washer at every end (NB0004, TA1606). 5. Tie T1 on the bottom posts, MB inside the left posts, T2 under the top posts (ties TA1897). 6. OLED: on the front of F1 on four 10 mm nylon standoffs (TA1040), M3 × 6 nylon bolts (TA1045) at both ends; its plug goes back through the slot. Speaker: 4 bolts, washers over the rim, nuts inside. Amp and GY-45 plug into carriers AC and GC (page 6): tie AC under T2, GC onto T1. Other boards: ties. 7. Solder the DevKit sockets on MB and wire it as on page 6. OLED and mic get plugs made from female header, amp and GY-45 sit in sockets, so every part still unplugs. Solder male headers (HE0002) to any board that comes without pins." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=8;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="1062" width="770" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="mainboard" name="6 · Main board wiring">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="0" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="1080" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="mainboardc1" value="KEY CUBE  ·  MAIN BOARD (MB) WIRING" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1100" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mainboardc2" value="The DevKit plugs into two 22-pin female sockets on a 74 × 40 Vero board. The amp and accelerometer sit in sockets on small carriers (AC, GC); the OLED and mic get plugs made from female header, so every part can be unplugged. Wires are soldered on the copper side of MB. Board drawn about 1.8 : 1, seen from the component side, front of the box on the left. All wire is 24 AWG circuit wire (black TA1176, red TA1177, green TA1178)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#555555;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="48" width="1100" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
