        <mxCell id="mainboardc80" value="Dashed lines are wires on the copper side: three buses (5V, 3V3, GND) run under J1, and the cables leave from the right-hand end of the board (z 66–68), between the bottom corner holes. Tip: plug both sockets onto the DevKit first, sit the DevKit + sockets on the board, then solder. The rows then line up exactly. Holes: the 4 corner holes (Ø3.2) take cable ties in the test frame and 5 mm standoffs (TA1037, hot-glued to the left panel, M3 × 6 nylon bolts TA1045) in the final box. Middle top hole: extra tie." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=8;fontColor=#1A1A1A;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="516" width="580" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
